.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.PP 

.SS "template<class Target>
.br
class cbor::encoder< Target >"Writes CBOR one data item per call, in the order of the bytes\&. 

The encoder counts nothing: the counts of \fR\fBarray\fP\fP and \fR\fBmap\fP\fP come from the program\&. The target is one of these:
.IP "\(bu" 2
a container of bytes, for example \fRstd::string\fP: the encoder appends; - a \fRstd::span\fP of bytes: the encoder writes into it and allocates nothing; - an \fBcbor::iov_writer\fP: the encoder gives pieces; - an object with \fRallocate(std::size_t)\fP, which gives a writer with \fRappend(std::string_view)\fP and \fRdone(std::size_t)\fP\&. The encoder does not write tags 28 and 29\&. Each call gives \fRstd::expected<void, \fBerror\fP>\fP\&. After an error, and after \fBcbor::encoder::finish()\fP, each call throws \fRstd::logic_error\fP\&. A copy does not compile\&.
.PP

.PP
.PP
.nf
cbor::encoder e(out)                     → encoder<std::string>
cbor::encoder e{std::span<char>(buffer)} → encoder<std::span<char>>
cbor::encoder e(w)                       → encoder<iov_writer>
.fi
.PP
 
.PP
.nf
bytes: a1 61 61 18 05
call: std::string out;
result: ""
call: cbor::encoder e(out);
result: encoder over a std::string
call: e\&.map(1)
result: void
call: e\&.text_string("a")
result: void
call: e\&.unsigned_integer(std::uint8_t{5})
result: void
call: e\&.finish()
result: 5
call: out
result: 5 bytes: a1 61 61 18 05

.fi
.PP

.PP
.PP
.nf
    std::string out;
    cbor::encoder e(out);
    bool const written = e\&.map(1) && e\&.text_string("a") && e\&.unsigned_integer(std::uint8_t{5});
    auto const size = e\&.finish();  // 5: out holds {"a": 5}, a1 61 61 18 05
.fi
.PP
 
